From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Araceae Runtime <runtime@araceae.invalid>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:05:40 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Recognize HTTP 2xx gateway error envelopes

Some model gateways answer a request with HTTP 200 and a JSON body shaped
like {"code": <non-zero>, "reason": "...", "message": "..."} instead of a
model response. A provider describes these envelopes under
[model_providers.<id>.error_envelope]:

- auth_failure_reasons: envelope reasons, compared after their last ".",
  that mean the credential was refused
- auth_failure_message_pattern: a regex over the envelope message with the
  same meaning
- auth_failure_statuses: additional HTTP statuses that count as refused
  credentials

Before stream parsing, the Responses endpoint reads a 2xx JSON body of up
to 1 MiB. A refused credential becomes an HTTP 401 transport error so
unauthorized recovery refreshes it; any other envelope fails the request
once as a non-retryable invalid request carrying the gateway reason and
message. Invalid patterns and statuses are rejected while loading
configuration.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
